---
// MapLibre's own stylesheet, linked so that it does not block first paint.
//
// ITS OWN COMPONENT BECAUSE OF WHERE IT HAS TO GO. It belongs in `<head>`, which means being
// written as a direct child of `<Base>` carrying `slot="head"` — a `slot` attribute inside a nested
// component's template is only an attribute. So each body page forwards it in one line:
//
//     <Fragment slot="head"><MapStylesheet /></Fragment>
//
// which beats two copies of the reasoning below.

// `?url` gives the emitted asset's href WITHOUT injecting the stylesheet, which is the whole point:
// a bare `import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css"` in the globe's client script made Vite hoist
// it into a render-blocking <link>, so **70 KB of widget CSS gated first paint** on a page where no
// widget exists until the 265 KB globe chunk has downloaded and run. Measured: FCP 1,264 -> 629 ms.
//
// Imported from the package, never copied into public/ — the version is pinned and guarded
// (vendoredPatches.test.ts), and a hand-copied stylesheet is the copy that silently stops matching.
import maplibreStylesheet from "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css?url";

// The onload body lives here as a STRING rather than inline on the element. Written inline, Astro
// type-checks the attribute as an expression and reports `ts(6133): 'media' is declared but its
// value is never read` — a hint about a variable that does not exist, on code the browser runs and
// the checker cannot model. `astro check` is held at zero, so a spurious hint costs the same as a
// real one: it trains the next reader to skim the output.
const PROMOTE_STYLESHEET = "this.media='all'";
---

{/* Non-blocking by `media="print"`: it matches no screen, so the parser does not wait on it, and
    the onload swap promotes it the moment it lands. Safe against the cascade because every one of
    our 26 overrides either beats the vendor rule on specificity or targets a different element —
    verified by reading computed styles off both orderings, not by argument.

    The <noscript> twin is not decoration. `onload` is an inline handler, so with JS off the sheet
    would stay `media="print"` forever and the controls would render unstyled. The globe needs JS
    anyway, but "needs JS" and "renders wrong without it" are different failures. */}
<link rel="stylesheet" href={maplibreStylesheet} media="print" onload={PROMOTE_STYLESHEET} />
<noscript>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href={maplibreStylesheet} />
</noscript>
